B.u59. {"problem": "Existing commits that passed their check before this change have checks_passed true and no checked_at. Under the new checks-pass rule they can no longer be approved until someone re-runs the check. The fixture C3 (checks_passed true, no checked_at) now behaves differently, and C1 (approved) lacks checked_at, so the world data is stale. The change adds no migration or backfill for this.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml: world.fixtures Commit C1/C3; approve_commit checks-pass", "kind": "behaviour", "from": "llm"}
B.u76. {"problem": "The diff re-sources the Commit object, record_check and approve_commit to interview line L56 with the original quotes removed, and sets status to proposed. The files after the change still show these elements as confirmed. approve_commit decides who may approve and its checks-pass precondition is a permission-type rule, which needs two people's confirmation. A confirmed status with no person's confirmation of the new freshness rule breaks the provenance rule. The Commit object is also now sourced to L56, while name_release and the stage transition still cite L53.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml: objects.Commit, actions.record_check, actions.approve_commit (checks-pass, source &id001)", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
