B.u82. {"problem": "The freshness rule is enforced only in approve_commit. The kernel-side record_approval precondition 'approved-only-if-checked' and the invariant 'approved-commits-passed-their-checks' still say only `checks_passed == true`, with no age limit. Their reasons and the glossary entry for 'change check' do not mention the one-day limit. A stale-but-passed commit can still be recorded as approved if the kernel-side step is reached later, so the rules are no longer consistent.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml: record_approval.approved-only-if-checked, invariants.approved-commits-passed-their-checks, glossary.change check", "kind": "contradiction", "from": "llm"}
