B.u77. {"problem": "The change introduces a `datetime` property type and the `now()` and `duration('24h')` functions in expressions. Nothing else in either domain uses them, so it is unverified that the compiler, the expression checker and the scenario harness support them. `now()` is also nondeterministic, so scenarios cannot reliably assert freshness.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml: Commit.checked_at, record_check effect, checks-pass check", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
B.u65. {"problem": "The freshness rule is enforced only on approve_commit. The kernel-side record_approval keeps its precondition approved-only-if-checked, which tests only checks_passed (or wording_only) and ignores checked_at. The invariant approved-commits-passed-their-checks has the same gap. A stale-checked commit can therefore still be recorded as approved, so 'checked only if less than a day old' does not hold across the domain. The glossary entry for 'change check' and the approval wording also do not mention the time limit.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, record_approval precondition approved-only-if-checked; invariant approved-commits-passed-their-checks", "kind": "contradiction", "from": "llm"}
B.u31. {"domain": "authoring", "check": "log_replay", "severity": "warning", "where": "7-f41dc2e7cb0f9a53@4", "problem": "record_check at 2026-11-09T16:34:47.877912+00:00 would now set ['checked_at'] differently", "carried": false, "from": "compiler"}
B.u64. {"problem": "The checks-pass precondition on approve_commit now needs checked_at, but the world fixture C3 has checks_passed: true and no checked_at. C3 used to be approvable and now is denied. The change did not update the fixture, and no scenario covers the freshness rule (a fresh check approves, a check over 24h old is denied).", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, world.fixtures Commit C3 and scenarios (approve-only-after-a-passing-check)", "kind": "reference", "from": "llm"}
